WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.686
Beginners mix up money words and then make bad decisions.

00:00:03.686 --> 00:00:07.741
You only need six: revenue, cost, profit, cash, price, and margin.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.689
This lesson is about money words without mba.

00:00:10.689 --> 00:00:12.901
Revenue, cost, profit, cash, price, margin.

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:15.481
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:19.167
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:24.696
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:25.016 --> 00:00:27.725
Revenue is the money customers pay you.

00:00:27.725 --> 00:00:33.918
If Maya sells one invoicing guide for seventy-nine dollars, revenue from that sale is seventy-nine dollars.

00:00:33.918 --> 00:00:37.402
Remember the objective: define revenue vs profit vs cash.

00:00:37.402 --> 00:00:41.659
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.659 --> 00:00:46.304
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:46.624 --> 00:00:49.106
Cost is what it takes to deliver.

00:00:49.106 --> 00:00:51.233
Maya tools might cost three dollars.

00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:55.487
Your time counts too - even when no cash leaves the bank.

00:00:55.487 --> 00:00:58.678
Remember the objective: define revenue vs profit vs cash.

00:00:58.678 --> 00:01:02.578
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:02.578 --> 00:01:06.832
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:07.152 --> 00:01:09.134
Profit is revenue minus cost.

00:01:09.134 --> 00:01:13.496
Seventy-nine minus three leaves seventy-six dollars before you count your time.

00:01:13.496 --> 00:01:17.064
Remember the objective: define revenue vs profit vs cash.

00:01:17.064 --> 00:01:21.426
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:21.426 --> 00:01:26.184
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:26.504 --> 00:01:27.543
Cash is different.

00:01:27.543 --> 00:01:29.967
Cash is money you can actually spend.

00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:34.815
You can show profit on paper and still be broke if payment is delayed.

00:01:34.815 --> 00:01:37.931
Remember the objective: define revenue vs profit vs cash.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:41.741
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:41.741 --> 00:01:45.896
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:46.216 --> 00:01:48.479
Price is what the buyer pays.

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:51.496
Margin is what remains after the unit cost.

00:01:51.496 --> 00:01:55.267
Use rough numbers early - precision theater delays first sales.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:58.662
Remember the objective: define revenue vs profit vs cash.

00:01:58.662 --> 00:02:02.810
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:07.336
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:02:07.656 --> 00:02:10.509
Remember: likes and empty waitlists are not cash.

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:16.572
Revenue comes in, cost goes out, profit is the gap, and cash is what you can use.

00:02:16.572 --> 00:02:19.781
Remember the objective: define revenue vs profit vs cash.

00:02:19.781 --> 00:02:23.704
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:02:23.704 --> 00:02:27.984
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:02:28.304 --> 00:02:33.453
In the quiz, you will separate revenue, profit, and cash in a new example.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:38.970
In the quiz, you will practice until you can define revenue vs profit vs cash.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:39.706
Answer carefully.

00:02:39.706 --> 00:02:43.016
If you miss one, review the idea and retry.

